ut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.2077em;\"><span class=\"overlay\" style=\"height:0.714em;width:0.471em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.471em\" height=\"0.714em\" style=\"width:0.471em\" viewBox=\"0 0 471 714\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin\"><path d=\"M377 20c0-5.333 1.833-10 5.5-14S391 0 397 0c4.667 0 8.667 1.667 12 5\n3.333 2.667 6.667 9 10 19 6.667 24.667 20.333 43.667 41 57 7.333 4.667 11\n10.667 11 18 0 6-1 10-3 12s-6.667 5-14 9c-28.667 14.667-53.667 35.667-75 63\n-1.333 1.333-3.167 3.5-5.5 6.5s-4 4.833-5 5.5c-1 .667-2.5 1.333-4.5 2s-4.333 1\n-7 1c-4.667 0-9.167-1.833-13.5-5.5S337 184 337 178c0-12.667 15.667-32.333 47-59\nH213l-171-1c-8.667-6-13-12.333-13-19 0-4.667 4.333-11.333 13-20h359\nc-16-25.333-24-45-24-59z\"/></svg></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.936em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.75em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.75em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5em;\"></span><span style=\"width:0.556em;height:3em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.556em\" height=\"3em\" viewBox=\"0 0 556 3000\"><path d=\"M145 15 v585 v1800 v585 c2.667,10,9.667,15,21,15\nc10,0,16.667,-5,20,-15 v-585 v-1800 v-585 c-2.667,-10,-9.667,-15,-21,-15\nc-10,0,-16.667,5,-20,15z M188 15 H145 v585 v1800 v585 h43z\nM367 15 v585 v1800 v585 c2.667,10,9.667,15,21,15\nc10,0,16.667,-5,20,-15 v-585 v-1800 v-585 c-2.667,-10,-9.667,-15,-21,-15\nc-10,0,-16.667,5,-20,15z M410 15 H367 v585 v1800 v585 h43z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.25em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><p>当所有个体朝向随机时 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi \\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ϕ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span></span>，当完全对齐时 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi = 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ϕ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span></span>。<span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\phi</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ϕ</span></span></span></span></span> 随某个控制参数（如交互半径、噪声强度）跨过临界值时会发生类似相变的骤升，这正是涌现「突然出现」的数学刻画。除序参量外，还可用空间熵衡量聚集程度、用互信息衡量个体间的统计耦合。这些指标让我们能客观比较两套规则谁的集体行为「更强」，而不必只靠看仿真动画。</p>\n<h2 id=\"简单个体-复杂群体-设计哲学\">简单个体，复杂群体：设计哲学</h2><p>群体机器人在工程上做的是一个反直觉的交换：主动放弃个体的强大，换取群体的可扩展与鲁棒。这条哲学有三层含义。其一，个体要便宜、可量产、可丢弃——损失百分之十的个体应当只损失约百分之十的性能，而非系统崩溃。其二，不依赖全局信息——任何需要「所有人都知道」的设计（如全局地图、统一时钟、中央调度器）都违背群体精神，因为它会重新引入单点故障与通信瓶颈，相关的去中心化原则见 <a href=\"../coordination/distributed-coordination\">分布式协调机制</a>。其三，规则要可复用——同一套靠近/对齐/避撞的规则既能做蜂拥又能做聚集，灵活性由此而来。</p>\n<p>这套哲学的灵感几乎全部来自生物：蚁群、蜂群、鸟群、鱼群用的正是「弱个体、强群体」的策略。生物如何用信息素、舞蹈与局部视野完成自组织，是 <a href=\"bio-inspired-self-organization\">生物启发与自组织</a> 的主题。</p>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><ul>\n<li>群体机器人 = 大量简单、同质、去中心化的个体，靠局部感知与局部交互产生协调集体行为。</li>\n<li>它区别于一般多机器人系统的核心是：个体弱、数量大、无全局信息、无中心控制。</li>\n<li>涌现是这门学科的根：宏观性质无法从单个个体直接推断，来自非线性局部交互的迭代。</li>\n<li>三大优势——可扩展、鲁棒、灵活——都源于「多」与「冗余」，而非个体强大。</li>\n<li>涌现可被量化（序参量、熵、互信息），从而让规则优劣可比较、可验证。</li>\n<li>设计哲学是用个体的简单换群体的强壮，而「从局部规则到全局行为」的反向映射是最难的工程问题，贯穿后续各章。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"群体智能与涌现","id":"群体智能与涌现"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念：什么是群体机器人","id":"核心概念-什么是群体机器人"},{"level":2,"text":"涌现：整体大于部分之和","id":"涌现-整体大于部分之和"},{"level":2,"text":"度量涌现：从有序到信息","id":"度量涌现-从有序到信息"},{"level":2,"text":"简单个体，复杂群体：设计哲学","id":"简单个体-复杂群体-设计哲学"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":null,"next":{"title":"生物启发与自组织","url":"/l-doc-books/h/robotics-automation/swarm-robotics/foundations/bio-inspired-self-organization"}}